That means we can come up with two different ways to find the area of $ACE.$ Setting them equal, we have: \begin{align*}
\frac{1}{2} \cdot AB \cdot CE &= \frac{1}{2} \cdot CD \cdot AE \\
AB \cdot CE &= CD \cdot AE \\
4 \cdot CE &= 8 \cdot 5 \\
